      "question_text": "Primary open-angle glaucoma: optic disc finding?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Papilledema",
        "B": "Increased cup-to-disc ratio (CDR >0.5)",
        "C": "Pale disc",
        "D": "Normal disc"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "POAG: progressive optic neuropathy. CDR >0.5 or asymmetry >0.2 is significant. Superotemporal and inferotemporal RNFL loss first → arcuate scotomas. Gradual, painless, peripheral vision loss."
